# Optimize & Write Less

Prefer small, focused edits. Reuse existing services, styles, and components. Do not rewrite working screens.

## Lists — FlatList first

Never use `.map()` for scrollable or table/list rows when `FlatList` fits.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
{items.map(item => <Row key={item.id} item={item} />)}

// ✅ GOOD
<FlatList
  data={items}
  keyExtractor={item => item.id}
  renderItem={renderItem}
  ListHeaderComponent={header}
  ListEmptyComponent={<Text>No items found.</Text>}
  initialNumToRender={10}
  windowSize={5}
/>
```

- Memoize `renderItem` / headers with `useCallback` / `useMemo`.
- Nested lists: `nestedScrollEnabled`, parent `scrollEnabled={false}` when needed.
- Always include `ListEmptyComponent` for empty data.

## API actions — lean wiring

- Put HTTP in `src/services/*`. Screen/handler: call service → update store only on success → surface the error on failure.
- Do not invent local-only delete/assign if an API exists.
- Drive UI from API flags instead of guessing from names/roles.

## Forms & pickers

- Field errors under each input + red border; clear on change.
- Searchable pickers: search input + `FlatList` + selected checkmark row.
- Include an empty option when selection is optional.

## Don't

- Don't add verbose comments, unused props, or parallel abstractions.
- Don't expand scope beyond the requested change.
- Don't replace working UI chrome unless asked.
